            <!-- SECTION 1: Introduction -->
            <h2>Section 1: Introduction — Why 50,000+ Patients Choose China Each Year</h2>

            <p class="lead">
                When my uncle couldn't walk more than 50 meters without excruciating knee pain, his local hospital quoted him $58,000 for a double knee replacement. He flew to Beijing instead. Six weeks later, he was walking pain-free through the Forbidden City. Total cost? $14,200. That's not a typo.
            </p>

            <p>Medical tourism to China for orthopedic procedures has grown 340% since 2019. What was once a whispered secret among those who couldn't afford Western healthcare is now a mainstream option for retirees, athletes, and anyone between a rock and a hard place with their knees.</p>

            <p>This guide covers everything you need to know about knee replacement surgery in China in 2026 — from costs and hospital comparisons to recovery timelines and the latest policy changes affecting international patients.</p>

            <div class="stats-grid">
                <div class="stat-card">
                    <div class="stat-number">50,000+</div>
