            <h2>Section 8: Risks and Mitigation — Being Realistic About Complications</h2>

            <p>No surgery is without risk. Here's an honest assessment of what can go wrong and how top Chinese hospitals minimize these risks:</p>

            <h3>Clinical Risks</h3>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h3>Risk 1: Infection</h3>
                <p><strong>Incidence:</strong> 0.5-1.2% at top Chinese hospitals (vs. 1-2% global average)</p>
                <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Pre-operative antibiotics administered 30-60 minutes before incision</li>
                    <li>Ultra-clean operating theaters with positive pressure ventilation</li>
                    <li>Antibiotic-impregnated cement used for implant fixation</li>
                    <li>Early mobilization protocols reduce post-op infection risk</li>
                    <li>24/7 infection monitoring during hospital stay</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>What to do if it happens:</strong> Treatment typically involves 6 weeks of IV antibiotics. Most infections are successfully treated without implant removal if caught early.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h3>Risk 2: Blood Clots (DVT/PE)</h3>
                <p><strong>Incidence:</strong> 0.5-1% at top hospitals with proper prophylaxis</p>
                <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Routine anticoagulation medications for 2-3 weeks post-op</li>
                    <li>Compression stockings and sequential compression devices</li>
                    <li>Early mobilization (walking by Day 1-2)</li>
                    <li>Hydration protocols</li>
                    <li>Pre-flight assessment includes D-dimer testing</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h3>Risk 3: Implant Loosening or Failure</h3>
                <p><strong>Incidence:</strong> 1-2% at 10 years (premium implants)</p>
                <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Use only FDA/CE approved implants from established manufacturers</li>
                    <li>Computer-navigated or robotic-assisted placement for precision</li>
                    <li>Appropriate implant selection for patient's age, weight, activity level</li>
                    <li>Patient education on activity restrictions during bone ingrowth period</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h3>Risk 4: Stiffness or Limited Range of Motion</h3>
                <p><strong>Incidence:</strong> 5-8% of patients require manipulation under anesthesia</p>
                <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Aggressive physiotherapy beginning Day 1 post-op</li>
                    <li>Continuous passive motion (CPM) machines provided</li>
                    <li>Patient compliance emphasized during rehab period</li>
                    <li>Regular range-of-motion assessments during follow-up</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h3>Non-Clinical Risks</h3>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h3>Risk 5: Language Barriers</h3>
                <p><strong>Mitigation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>All recommended hospitals have dedicated international departments</li>
                    <li>English-speaking nurses assigned to international patient floors</li>
                    <li>24/7 coordinator available by phone/WeChat/WhatsApp</li>
                    <li>All consent forms and discharge instructions provided in English</li>
