            <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>

            <h3>How long do I need to stay in China?</h3>
            <p>Plan for 2-3 weeks. Surgery on day 2-3, hospital stay 5-7 days, then 7-10 days of outpatient physiotherapy and follow-ups before flying home.</p>

            <h3>Will my insurance cover it?</h3>
            <p>Some international insurers cover overseas treatment. Check with your provider. Many patients use the savings to pay out-of-pocket and still come out ahead.</p>

            <h3>What about the implants? Are they safe?</h3>
            <p>Top hospitals use FDA-approved implants from Zimmer, Stryker, DePuy - the same brands used in Western hospitals. You can request specific brands.</p>

            <h3>Can I get both knees done at once?</h3>
            <p>Yes, bilateral knee replacement is common. Recovery is slightly longer, but you only make one trip. Most patients choose this option.</p>

            <h3>What if something goes wrong after I return home?</h3>
            <p>Complications are rare, but hospitals provide 24/7 remote consultation. Your local orthopedic surgeon can handle most issues using the detailed discharge records provided.</p>

            <h3>How do I verify surgeon credentials?</h3>
            <p>Ask the hospital for your surgeon's CV, including international training, number of procedures performed, and publication history. Top hospitals are transparent about surgeon qualifications.</p>

            <h3>What's not included in the quoted price?</h3>
            <p>Typically not included: flights, accommodation, meals, travel insurance, and any treatment for pre-existing conditions discovered during pre-op workup.</p>

